-DFlash truncation. It does not read production source text.
+DFlash truncation. Its two-token committed-stop case drives the production
+output-loop action: the first terminal token requires `EMIT_NEXT`, the second
+is emitted and then yields `RELEASE`, and any additional output is rejected.
+It does not read production source text.
 
